From: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell: use the variadic readline message prototype

The readline header exposes the variadic rl_message prototype when
USE_VARARGS and PREFER_STDARG are defined. Enable those declarations so
modern compilers accept BlueZ's formatted rl_message calls.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/shared/shell.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/shared/shell.c b/src/shared/shell.c
--- a/src/shared/shell.c
+++ b/src/shared/shell.c
@@ -36,0 +37,2 @@
+#define USE_VARARGS
+#define PREFER_STDARG
